# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ holds ~4.5 GB of .npy spectrograms and generated YOLO datasets -- none
# of that belongs in git. But a handful of small CSVs in there are the exact
# opposite: hand-made, irreproducible, and text.
#
# The review_status.csv files in particular are hundreds of hours of human
# judgement (624 reviews / 343 manual burst-time corrections as of 2026-08-12)
# and existed on exactly one disk with no version control until now. They are
# also the only place that history lives at all: review_store.py overwrites a
# record in place when an event is re-reviewed and keeps no audit trail, so a
# git commit is what makes "when did this label change, and from what" a
# question that can be answered.
#
# Note the ignore/re-include ladder below: git will not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so `!data/x/y.csv` alone silently does nothing. Each
# level has to exclude its *contents* (`dir/*`) while leaving the directory
# itself includable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/ecallisto/
!data/burst_data/

data/ecallisto/*
!data/ecallisto/raw_events/
!data/ecallisto/windows/

data/ecallisto/raw_events/*
!data/ecallisto/raw_events/review_status.csv
!data/ecallisto/raw_events/metadata.csv

# windows.csv / boxes.csv are regenerable (detection/refresh_boxes.py, no
# download needed) but are tracked anyway: they pin which dataset a given
# result was produced from. The .bak-* copies refresh_boxes writes are not.
data/ecallisto/windows/*
!data/ecallisto/windows/windows.csv
!data/ecallisto/windows/boxes.csv

data/burst_data/*
!data/burst_data/rough_events/
data/burst_data/rough_events/*
!data/burst_data/rough_events/review_status.csv
!data/burst_data/rough_events/metadata.csv

burst_data.zip

# Training runs: weights + plots, 1.1 GB and fully reproducible from the
# scripts + the tracked CSVs above.
detection/runs/
*.log

# Redundant now that the CSVs themselves are versioned -- git history is the
# backup. Kept on disk, just not committed.
event_review/backups/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Checkpoints / model weights
*.pth
*.pt
checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
